  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "you're asked for depth at the end, not the actual folder path - do you need to remember folder names at all, or just how many levels deep you are?",
    "\"../\" decreases depth by one but never below zero, \"./\" does nothing, and anything else increases depth by one",
    "split logs on spaces and walk through the tokens, updating a single depth counter",
    "the answer is just the final depth counter value"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "letting depth go negative when \"../\" is used at the main folder instead of clamping at zero",
    "building a full explicit stack of folder names when a simple integer counter suffices (not wrong, just unnecessary overhead)",
    "mis-splitting the logs string, e.g. not handling the trailing slash correctly when tokenizing"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A file system crawler starts in the main folder and processes a\nspace-delimited sequence of navigation operations, `logs`. Each token is\none of: \"../\" (move to the parent folder, or stay in the main folder if\nalready there), \"./\" (stay in the current folder, no effect), or any\nother token (move into a subfolder with that name, creating a deeper\nlevel).\n\n**After processing every operation in order, return the minimum number of \"../\" operations needed to get back to the main folder.**\n\nThat minimum is simply how many levels deep the crawler ended up.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= number of tokens in logs <= 1000",
      "1 <= each token's length <= 10",
      "each token is \"../\", \"./\", or lowercase letters/digits naming a subfolder"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "logs that try to go above the main folder with extra \"../\" tokens",
      "logs made entirely of \"./\" (depth never changes)",
      "a single subfolder move with no other operations"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "logs = \"d1/ d2/ ../ ../ d21/ ./ d3/\"",
        "output": "2",
        "expectedOutput": "2",
        "explanation": "depth 0 -> d1/ depth1 -> d2/ depth2 -> ../ depth1 -> ../ depth0 -> d21/ depth1 -> ./ depth1 (no change) -> d3/ depth2"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "logs = \"d1/ ../ ../ ../\"",
        "output": "0",
        "expectedOutput": "0",
        "explanation": "depth 0 -> d1/ depth1 -> ../ depth0 -> ../ depth0 (already at main, no-op) -> ../ depth0 (still no-op)"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "logs = \"d1/ d2/ d3/ ../ d31/\"",
        "output": "3",
        "expectedOutput": "3",
        "explanation": "depth 0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> ../ depth2 -> d31/ depth3"
      }
    ],
